{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Rachel as well as Leah.</b> The intent is that he loved Leah, but Rachel more. And this is contrary to the way of the world, to love more the woman a man knew first, as our Sages of blessed memory expounded: 'a woman does not enter into covenant except with one who has made her a vessel.' And because this love was not after the way of all the earth, he added and said, <b>Rachel as well</b>. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:18.511176973Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}